    {
      "id": 16,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "What this dashboard can and cannot show",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 10,
        "x": 14,
        "y": 25
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**There is no per-device domain breakdown here, and that is a limitation of the exporter rather than an oversight.**\n\n`raylas/nextdns-exporter` attaches a device label to exactly one metric, `nextdns_device_queries`. Domains, query types, protocols, destinations, DNSSEC and encryption are all collected profile-wide with no device dimension, so they cannot be filtered to a single device.\n\nThe NextDNS API itself *does* accept a `device` parameter on its analytics endpoints. Surfacing top domains per device would mean running a modified exporter that queries those endpoints once per device.\n\nEverything above is derived from query volume and timing, which is what the current metrics support."
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {},
        "overrides": []
      },
      "transparent": false
    }
